\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come, Holy Ghost, all-quickening fire,
\par Come, and in me delight to rest;
\par Drawn by the lure of strong desire,
\par O come and consecrate my breast;
\par The temple of my soul prepare,
\par And fix Thy sacred presence there.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Eager for Thee I ask and pant;
\par So strong, the principle divine
\par Carrries me out, with sweet constraint,
\par Till all my hallowed soul is Thine;
\par Plunged in the Godhead's deepest sea,
\par And lost in Thine immensity.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. My peace, my life, my comfort Thou,
\par My treasure and my all Thou art;
\par True witness of my sonship, now
\par Engraving pardon on my heart,
\par Seal of my sins in Christ forgiven,
\par Earnest of love, and pledge of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Come then, my God, mark out Thine heir,
\par Of heaven a larger earnest give;
\par With clearer light Thy witness bear,
\par More sensibly within me live;
\par Let all my powers Thine entrance feel,
\par And deeper stamp Thyself the seal.
\par \tab\tab\tab Amen.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

